A||||5||VAROOM||one vacume line left||||5
Z||000000||VAROOM||11-21-1999||11:00 AM||||On my 87 GT, at the bottom of the air filter assembly there is a fitting for a vacume line. My question is , where does this thing hook up??. where to, and for what. Ithink this might finally fix this 2.8 thing. Thanks.   ||||reg||5
Z||000001||David||11-21-1999||11:46 AM||||Sounds like it is the vacuum line that controls the flapper door in the air filter to allow heat from the exhaust manifold to pre-heat the air going into the engine.  This gives better performance during warm-up.  The line would go to a vacuum source somewhere on the intake manifold.  The V6 people can help you with exactly where it goes, mine was a 4 cly.||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||11-21-1999||10:48 PM||||V6 don't have a preheat pipe like the early 4 cyls do. 87-88 4 cyls don't have it either. But a vacuum line to the air filter??? I don't think Ive ever seen one on the canister. Might be a left over from recall days... Will have to look at mine when the sun comes out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||11-21-1999||11:44 PM||||On bottom of the air cleaner? you sure it's not a moisture drain? I don't know of anything that has a small line to the air cleaner. you wouldn't get any vacuum there, but you could use it for a clean air intake for something.<P>The PCV intake line goes to a large fitting usually on an elbow near the cleaner.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Carrolles||11-22-1999||12:02 AM||||A vacuum hose connects between this and a steel tube that runs along the firewall to near the battery.  On that end another vacuum hose connects from there to the filter port of the EGR vacuum servo.||||reg||1
Z||000005||ka4nkf||11-22-1999||12:10 AM||||Sounds like this is the fresh air hose for the EGR control switch. it is located in front of the thermostat housing.||||reg||1
